## **7.1  Booth****'****s Multiplier — Test Cases**

The following table presents signed 23-bit test cases used to verify the multiplier. Results are split into High bits (upper 23 bits) and Low bits (lower 23 bits) of the 46-bit product.

| **M (Multiplicand)** | **Q (Multiplier)** | **Expected Product** | **Type** | **Result** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| +6  (0x000006) | +5  (0x000005) | +30  (0x00001E) | Positive × Positive | Pass |
| −6  (0xFFFFFA) | +5  (0x000005) | −30  (0xFFFFE2) | Negative × Positive | Pass |
| +7  (0x000007) | −3  (0xFFFFFD) | −21  (0xFFFFEB) | Positive × Negative | Pass |
| −4  (0xFFFFFC) | −4  (0xFFFFFC) | +16  (0x000010) | Negative × Negative | Pass |
| +0  (0x000000) | +127(0x00007F) | +0   (0x000000) | Zero multiplicand | Pass |
| +1  (0x000001) | +1  (0x000001) | +1   (0x000001) | Identity | Pass |

## **7.2  ALU — Function Verification**

| **Operation** | **A Input** | **B Input** | **Expected Result** | **Flags Checked** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| AND | 0x0F0F0F | 0xFF00FF | 0x0F000F | Zero=0, Neg=0 |
| OR | 0x0F0F0F | 0xF0F0F0 | 0xFFFFFF | Zero=0, Neg=1 |
| ADD | 0x3FFFFF | 0x000001 | 0x400000 | Overflow=1, Carry=0 |
| SUB | 0x000005 | 0x000005 | 0x000000 | Zero=1 |
| SUB | 0x000000 | 0x000001 | 0xFFFFFF | Neg=1, Overflow=0 |

## **7.3  CPU — Sample Program Trace**

A sample program was loaded into the RAM block to verify fetch-decode-execute across multiple instructions:

| **PC** | **Instruction** | **Assembly** | **Ac Before** | **Ac After** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 0x00000 | 0xC00014 | LDA [0x14] | 0x000000 | 0x000019 (+25) |
| 0x00001 | 0x20000B | ADD [0x0B] | 0x000019 | 0x000024 (+36) |
| 0x00002 | 0x80000C | STO [0x0C] | 0x000024 | 0x000024 (unchanged) |
| 0x00003 | 0xE00000 | HLT | 0x000024 | 0x000024 (halted) |

The mem[0x14] contained 0x000019 (+25) and mem[0x0B] contained 0x00000B (+11). After ADD, Ac correctly holds +36 (0x000024). The STO instruction writes this back to mem[0x0C], verified by inspecting the RAM contents post-execution.

## **7.4  Observed Waveforms**

Using Logisim's simulation step-by-step mode (Ctrl+T), the following behaviours were observed and verified:

- Booth multiplier: BUSY remains HIGH for exactly 23 clock ticks (counter max = 0x17), then falls LOW. High bits and Low bits simultaneously become valid.

- Shift registers A, Q, and Q-1 update correctly each cycle. The sign bit of A is preserved during arithmetic right-shift (confirming arithmetic, not logical, shift).

- The ControlUnit's uPC counter increments through the correct micro-sequence for each instruction and resets to the fetch state at the end of each instruction.

- MAR and MBR assert/deassert in sync with R and W signals. No bus conflicts were observed (no red wires in Logisim simulation).

- The zero flag correctly asserts when the ALU result is 0x000000, verified for SUB A−A.

